<title>NORWAY: Christiania Bank 9-month profits fall.</title>
<headline>Christiania Bank 9-month profits fall.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>None months to September 30.</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Net interest income		 2,562     vs     2,472</p>
<p>Total non-interest income	 1,085     vs	 952</p>
<p>Total non-interest expenses     2,247     vs     2,167</p>
<p>Operating profit before loan</p>
<p>		 losses/reversals   1,400     vs     1,257</p>
<p>Losses/reversals			131     vs     1,062</p>
<p>Operating result before tax     1,566     vs     2,322</p>
<p>Result after tax		    1,550     vs     2,324</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's second largest bank is Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA. A Reuter poll of eight analysts forecast net profits of 1.54 billion crowns for the first nine months and an operating profit before loan losses/reversals of 1.44 billion crowns. Four of the analysts recommended a buy on the share, two said hold, one said sell and one decline to comment.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
